Host [Socket]
Type in the IP address of the computer with which you want to establish the connection.
The IP address of the Host connects to the host computer.
• For a client socket the Host sets the IP address of the host computer to which the Socket Interface is to
establish the connection. The number 127.0.0.1 designates the local host.
• For a server socket the Host sets the IP address on which the server is waiting for incoming connections.
If the text box is empty or contains the value 127.0.0.1 incoming connections on all network interfaces
are allowed.
